{"name":"Little Princess","hex":"#e6aac1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"little","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Small, not large, limited, particularly:","Small, limited in size."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Not much.","Not at all."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/little"},{"term":"princess","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A female member of a royal family other than a queen, especially a daughter or granddaughter of a monarch. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A woman or girl who excels in a given field or class."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/princess"}],"entries":[{"title":"A Little Princess","blocks":[{"text":"A Little Princess is a work by British-American author Frances Hodgson Burnett, presented as a 1888 novella, a 1902 play and a 1905 children's novel. All three versions tell the story of Sara Crewe, a wealthy young girl and the prize student of a private London boarding school who is reduced to poverty and forced to endure the life of a servant under the school's cruel headmistress."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/A_Little_Princess_cover.jpg/330px-A_Little_Princess_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/A_Little_Princess","wikidata":"Q10483376"},{"title":"A Little Princess (musical)","blocks":[{"text":"A Little Princess, The Musical is a musical with music by Andrew Lippa and book and lyrics by Brian Crawley, based on the 1905 children's novel of the same name by Frances Hodgson Burnett."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/A_Little_Princess_(musical)","wikidata":"Q16959877"},{"title":"Little Princess (British TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Little Princess is a British animated children's television series created by The Illuminated Film Company. It was directed by Edward Foster during series 1–3 and directed by Sue Tong during series 4. It premiered in the United Kingdom in 2006. The programme is shown in the UK as part of Channel 5's Milkshake! and as Y Dywysoges Fach in the children's programming strand Cyw on the Welsh language channel S4C."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Little_Princess_(British_TV_series)","wikidata":"Q1570778"},{"title":"Princess","blocks":[{"text":"Princess is a title used by a female member of a regnant monarch's family or by a female ruler of a principality. The male equivalent is a prince. Most often, the term has been used for the consort of a prince, or for the daughter of a monarch. A crown princess can be the heir apparent to the throne or the spouse of the heir apparent."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Sigrid_Eriksdotter_Vasa.jpg/330px-Sigrid_Eriksdotter_Vasa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Princess","wikidata":"Q863048"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/The_Little_Princess_1903_Playibill.png/500px-The_Little_Princess_1903_Playibill.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/The_Little_Princess_1903_Playibill.png/500px-The_Little_Princess_1903_Playibill.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Little_Princess_1903_Playibill.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Sara_Crewe%3B_or%2C_What_happened_at_Miss_Minchin%27s_%281888%29_%2814781217922%29.jpg/500px-Sara_Crewe%3B_or%2C_What_happened_at_Miss_Minchin%27s_%281888%29_%2814781217922%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Sara_Crewe%3B_or%2C_What_happened_at_Miss_Minchin%27s_%281888%29_%2814781217922%29.jpg/1280px-Sara_Crewe%3B_or%2C_What_happened_at_Miss_Minchin%27s_%281888%29_%2814781217922%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Sara_Crewe%3B_or%2C_What_happened_at_Miss_Minchin%27s_%281888%29_%2814781217922%29.jpg/500px-Sara_Crewe%3B_or%2C_What_happened_at_Miss_Minchin%27s_%281888%29_%2814781217922%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"She Slowly Advanced into the Parlor, Clutching Her Doll: Illustration by Reginald B. Birch from Sara Crewe; or, What Happened at Miss Minchin's (1888)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASara_Crewe%3B_or%2C_What_happened_at_Miss_Minchin's_(1888)_(14781217922).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/A_Little_Princess_djvu-p123.png/500px-A_Little_Princess_djvu-p123.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/A_Little_Princess_djvu-p123.png/1280px-A_Little_Princess_djvu-p123.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/A_Little_Princess_djvu-p123.png/500px-A_Little_Princess_djvu-p123.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"She seldom cried. She did not cry now. 1905 illustration by Ethel Franklin Betts from A Little Princess (1917 edition).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AA_Little_Princess_djvu-p123.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/A_Little_Princess_djvu-p267.png/500px-A_Little_Princess_djvu-p267.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/A_Little_Princess_djvu-p267.png/1280px-A_Little_Princess_djvu-p267.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src"